FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
 value : DWORD;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT ...
END_VAR
VAR
 previousValue : DWORD := DWORD#0;
 workMask : DWORD;
 bitIndex : USINT; perhaps loop issue USINT overflow at 255 not here. Use INT or USINT.
END_VAR

Implementation:
risingBits := value AND NOT previousValue;
fallingBits := previousValue AND NOT value;
hasChanged := value <> previousValue;
hasRisingEdges := risingBits <> DWORD#0;
...
noOf... := 0;
workMask := risingBits;
FOR bitIndex := 0 TO 31 DO
  IF (workMask AND DWORD#1) <> DWORD#0 THEN noOfRisingBits := noOfRisingBits + USINT#1; END_IF;
  workMask := SHR(workMask, 1);
END_FOR;
Then falling reuse. previousValue := value.

Potential issue output count USINT addition expression accepted. CODESYS FOR control var INT. Use bitIndex : INT. `SHR(workMask, 1)` standard. Counts max32. Fine.

Can combine one pass over both masks using riseWork/fallWork. Should have all VAR sections. No VAR_IN_OUT etc.

Should previousValue initialized explicit. JSON escaping newlines. supporting_objects [].

